{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Celebrating Christmas", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Remember the Time ... ?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 18, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Used to and Would to Talk About Past Habits", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Used to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">would</span> are both used to talk about past actions.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Gerry</span>: What did you use to do with your families on Christmas when you were young?</br> <span class=\"strong\">Ana</span>: We used to go skating. We would open our presents, then head to the Boston Common skating rink. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> to express something that we often did in the past, but don't do anymore. It is often used to talk about something that was a habit, or a way of life in the past. We use it to contrast past habits with present situations.</br> <span class=\"strong\">Used to</span>  can refer to situations as well as habitual actions.</p> We use <span class=\"strong\">would</span> to talk about past actions and habits as well.</br>  Would  only refers to actions, but not situations.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I used to skate.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I don't skate anymore.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I would skate all day long.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It was my habit to spend all day skating.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Present Perfect Tense versus The Simple Past Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a finished action or event that is connected to the present in some way.</p>  You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished action or event <span class=\"strong\">not</span> connected to the present.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "I haven't had a Christmas like this one for a while.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Have you ever heard of the Freedom Trail? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We've made our own traditions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Gilly, Teddy and I wrote and performed plays for Christmas.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We put together costumes and wrote out dialogues. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We rehearsed for hours.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Look at the chart about how to form the Present Perfect tense:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">have/has</span> + <span class=\"strong\">the past participle</span> of the verb in Present Perfect sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Base Form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"hear\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"heard\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"heard\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Have you ever heard ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"make\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"made\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"made\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We haven't had ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I have had ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"been\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They have been ...\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to go skating", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to move around ice wearing skates", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We went skating at the local arena. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about Christmas.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to race around", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to run all over", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The children race around the house laughing and squealing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to follow", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to move behind someone or something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We followed the Freedom Trail. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to give someone a break", "type